<title>USA: TABLE - Pittsburgh Home Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Pittsburgh Home Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ended  Nine months ended</p>
<p>				    June 30,	     June 30,</p>
<p>			     1997	1996	  1997	 1996</p>
<p>Total interest income</p>
<p>			4,679,422  3,254,883  12,901,285  9,331,397</p>
<p>Total interest expense</p>
<p>			2,829,473  1,780,760   7,624,146  5,529,434</p>
<p>Net interest income before</p>
<p>provision for loan losses</p>
<p>			1,849,949  1,474,123   5,277,139  3,801,963</p>
<p>Provision for loan losses</p>
<p>			  105,000     90,000     255,000    210,000</p>
<p>Net interest income after</p>
<p>provision for loan losses</p>
<p>			1,744,949  1,384,123   5,022,139  3,591,963</p>
<p>Total noninterest income</p>
<p>			  227,105     90,500     425,673    270,447</p>
<p>Total noninterest expense</p>
<p>			1,098,499    908,278   3,259,702  2,557,056</p>
<p> Income taxes	 326,300    197,175     775,300    474,575</p>
<p> Net income	   547,255    369,170   1,412,810    830,779</p>
<p> Earnings per share    0.30	 0.18	  0.75	  N/A</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said the rise in net income for current Q3 primarily reflects an increase in net interest income.</p>
<p>Earnings per share information not applicable for nine months 1996 as the company completed its stock offering in April 1996.</p>
<p>The company said per share results for both periods of 1997 were helped by a reduction in shares outstanding due to stock repurchase programs in effect from November 1996 through April 1997; The company repurchased 109,106 shares during Q1 1997 and an additional 103,650 shares between February and April 1997, it said.</p>
<p>Full company name is Pittsburgh Home Financial Corp.</p>
